WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:02.670
- [Narrator] One tweet is putting at risk

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:06.200
the NBA's multi-billion-dollar
opportunity in China,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.090
while upsetting basketball
fans at home and abroad.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.610
It was sparked when Houston
Rockets general manager

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.341
Daryl Morey tweeted his support
for Hong Kong protesters.

00:00:15.341 --> 00:00:18.290
(crowd chanting)

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:20.890
The NBA stands out from
other U.S. companies

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:23.210
in that it didn't kowtow
to China's pressure,

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:24.890
whereas other companies have.

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:26.280
- They'll say, "Sorry,"

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:28.450
they'll express regret at what's happened.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:29.800
The idea is for them to get

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.480
their relationships with the Chinese.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:33.010
What's been interesting with the NBA

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.280
is this backlash from American consumers

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.130
has made that much more
difficult for them.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:39.040
- [Narrator] This dilemma
is heightened even more

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.360
as China could overtake
the U.S. as the world's

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.970
largest retail market
as soon as this year.

00:00:43.970 --> 00:00:46.530
So can U.S. brands reconcile its values

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.080
and Chinese money?
(camera clicking)

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.860
The Houston Rockets are one of the most

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:53.430
popular NBA teams in China.

00:00:53.430 --> 00:00:55.450
Chinese basketball legend Yao Ming

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.980
spent his entire NBA career in Houston.

00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.610
- A lot of American companies have made

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.150
a really big deal out of
China in the past few years.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:04.270
It's that sort of premier growth market,

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:06.120
it's where they see a
lot of their expansion

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.160
in the coming years.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:09.110
- [Narrator] Today, China has 300 million

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:10.400
basketball players,

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.260
nearly as many people
as there are in the U.S.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.820
In July, Chinese tech giant Tencent,

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.740
which is the official
broadcaster of NBA games,

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.530
paid at least $1.5 billion to extend

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:23.470
its streaming deal with the league.

00:01:23.470 --> 00:01:25.840
The team tried to distance
themselves from Morey,

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.160
who said he didn't mean to offend anyone,

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:29.600
but the damage was done.

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:31.720
Billions of dollars are now at stake.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.480
Chinese companies, sponsors,

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.440
and the Chinese Basketball Association

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:37.720
suspended ties with the Rockets.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:40.500
The national TV broadcaster
decided to not air

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:43.510
two upcoming NBA games and
said it would reconsider

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:45.320
its partnership with the league.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.620
- Tencent reported that
490 million Chinese people

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:52.470
had watched an NBA
basketball game last year.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.880
That's a huge deal.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.470
- [Narrator] The NBA's initial response

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.280
called Morey's tweet regrettable,

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.980
but that drew swift criticism
from U.S. politicians

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:02.091
on both sides of the aisle.

00:02:02.091 --> 00:02:04.841
(dramatic music)

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.600
- The usual way that U.S.
companies navigate through,

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.500
and this is true of companies
outside the U.S. as well,

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:13.330
is to give in, effectively.

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:16.300
They'll apologize or back
down in whatever way they can

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.770
without breaking laws
in their home country.

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:21.030
- [Narrator] In June, Nike
withdrew a shoe collection

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.490
in China after its
codesigner brand supported

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.390
the Hong Kong protesters' demand to kill

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:28.190
an extradition bill that
sparked the protests.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:30.940
The luxury retailer Tiffany
apologized for a tweet

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.940
that Chinese netizens
saw as pro-Hong Kong.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.340
Covering the right eye has become

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:37.210
a symbol of police brutality

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.713
after a woman was shot
in the eye by police.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.730
The NBA took a different stance.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:45.780
- We are not apologizing

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:50.130
for Daryl exercising his
freedom of expression.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:51.500
- What they're facing is the difficulty

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.670
between their U.S. base of consumers,

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.740
who don't really want them to apologize

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:59.960
for expressing an opinion on Hong Kong,

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.340
against their new Chinese consumers.

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.670
They've faced a clash
between the two groups.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:06.050
- [Narrator] The NBA is discovering

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:08.640
that it's impossible to have it both ways.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:11.280
The league's strong brand in
the U.S. could be tarnished

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.180
if its executives are seen
to be in Beijing's pocket.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:15.840
- I think it's gonna be
completely impossible

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.670
to avoid these scandals completely.

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:19.240
Essentially, it's balancing

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.280
the freedom of speech of your employees

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.620
and the people associated
with your company

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.310
against what Beijing wants

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:27.772
in your fastest-growing growth market.

00:03:27.772 --> 00:03:31.182
(shoes squeaking)
(people chattering)

